       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. At that dose the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's long half-life would make any overdose effect last a long time.\n\nPlease check whether one of these was intended:\n- **5 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose. Some patients, such as frail or older ones or those with hepatic impairment, start at 2.5 mg.\n- **10 mg once daily**, the maximum recommended dose.\n- A typo or a different drug, or a different unit.\n\nIf 50 mg is deliberate, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note documenting that you confirmed it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
