       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. Amlodipine 50 mg daily is well above the 10 mg maximum, and I don't know of any indication that supports it. In a 70 kg patient with normal kidney and liver function, it risks serious harm. I also can't tell a deliberate dose from a slip, because the confirmation came without a clinical rationale.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Change the dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily right away. If the goal is stronger blood pressure control, I can also enter an additional agent from another class.\n- **Get a second check.** If you think a dose above the label maximum is warranted, discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. They can enter it or authorize it through your institution's override process.\n\nTell me the dose you'd like and I'll enter it."
